  "answer": "Based on the research, here's the answer:\n\n## Countries Meeting All Criteria\n\n**Only 1 country: Finland**\n\n---\n\n### Cross-Reference Analysis\n\n| IQ Air 2023 WHO-Compliant Countries (PM2.5 ≤ 5 µg/m³) | 2022 EPI Sanitation & Drinking Water Rank 1 | 2022 EPI Water Resources Rank 1 | **Both EPI Ranks = 1** |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Australia | No | No | No |\n| Estonia | No | No | No |\n| **Finland** | **Yes (tied 100.00)** | **Yes (tied 100.00)** | **YES** |\n| Grenada | No | No | No |\n| Iceland | Yes (tied 100.00) | No | No |\n| Mauritius | No | No | No |\n| New Zealand | No | No | No |\n\n---\n\n### Key Findings\n\n- **7 sovereign countries** met WHO PM2.5 standards in IQ Air 2023: Australia, Estonia, Finland, Grenada, Iceland, Mauritius, New Zealand [1][2]\n- **2022 EPI Sanitation & Drinking Water** rank 1 (tied): Norway, Switzerland, Netherlands, Finland, UK, Iceland [3]\n- **2022 EPI Water Resources** rank 1 (tied): Denmark, Finland [3]\n- **Finland** is the only country appearing on all three lists\n\n---\n\n## Sources\n\n[1] IQAir 2023 World Air Quality Report press release — https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/2023-iqair-world-air-quality-report-finds-only-7-countries-meet-who-pm2-5-air-pollution-guideline-302088419.html\n\n[2] Full 2023 IQAir report (Greenpeace-hosted PDF) — https://www.greenpeace.org/static/planet4-india-stateless/2024/03/44a856c8-2023_world_air_quality_report.pdf\n\n[3] EPI 2022 component rankings — https://epi.yale.edu/epi-results/2022/component/h2o (Sanitation & Drinking Water) and https://epi.yale.edu/epi-results/2022/component/wrs (Water Resources)",
